# Navigation

Desktop/tablet have exactly one global navigation layer. Canonical destinations: Messages, My Work, Projects, ◆ Vimla, Settings.

Never put recent conversations, folders, tasks, notes, reminders, lists, favorites, archive or project lists in the global sidebar.

List/detail is drill-down:
- Messages -> separate conversation page
- Projects -> separate project page
- Notes/Lists -> separate detail page

Issue #15: Messages use a persistent local conversation-list pane alongside detail at ≥1024px and route-selected single panes below it. The list is not a second global navigation layer.

Issue #17: normal Projects routes use the same approved drill-down architecture: a persistent local project-list pane alongside project detail at ≥1024px, and route-selected list/detail panes below it. `/projects/join` remains a focused flow. The project list is never global navigation. See `docs/CONSUMER_LAYOUT.md`.

My Work local nav: Today / Tasks / Reminders / Lists / Notes.
Project local nav: Overview / Chats / Work / Context / Members. It remains inside project detail content rather than becoming another global sidebar.

Mobile bottom nav has exactly Messages / My Work / Projects / Vimla. Settings/profile via account UI.

Do not create fake production routes for future features. Use real feature gates or dev-only presentation until the roadmap phase implements them.
